    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d57">

                <pb facs="0297" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1820</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-27T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1915, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.45 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>304. No declaration of war yet with Germany but when German Embassy demanded
                    passports its Counselor stated that probably German troops would be found with
                    Austrians on the frontier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
